eeded"],["6ae5b94c_9a2bae0f",32,-1,1,"This makes me wonder if we should have a ShouldMoveIntersectionStartForward, as well"],["7fdfd9af_73858583",32,-1,1,"Can it ever be beyond if the while loop above is `(start < last_intersection_index)`?"],["a6e33810_3795bb4f",32,-1,1,"nit: I'd place this first, since if it evaluates to true, it will be slightly faster than the first evaluation rule before it"],["f24db2b3_0f8771e5",32,-1,1,"nit: const"],["08e5e5d1_83def000",32,0,1,"nit: This check should be implied by the above if-statement, so this check can be removed"],["3792dfa5_f196c0eb",32,0,1,"nit: I might move this to the first part of the if, since I'd guess it is slightly faster, and also means that we don't get the blocked_status and might not actually need it (for example, if…"]],0,173],[7133118,20410,128,4.229,3.289,[[1,0.985,127,128],[0,0.015,75,0]],[["1cad74fb_2cb3fedc",14,-1,1,"Why do we have this piece of code in each? Is this an artifact of the original generated inherit method?"],["313fc345_e1e24cf1",14,-1,1,"nit: I'd add a comment here and in the other methods to provide more details for future context"],["e20b5340_af7358f0",22,-1,1,"nit: can you add details on what the actual issue was? i.e. that the change is not taking effect when inherited?"],["fad8c48f_3bdb3895",22,-1,1,"nit: I'd add a separate line break here to put this in a separate paragraph"]],0,174]]}